{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPrivate compatibility aliases remain for CLI help routing, `run_security_detectors`, graph/reducer symbols, split reducer processors, and grounding `DIMENSIONS`. Their consumers are internal source or test/monkeypatch paths; no public wire or persisted-data contract requires them. The governing ADR is delivered by earthen-wheat-chick.\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the ADR merges, migrate all consumers to `_help_route`, `run_detectors`, graph loader/reducer canonical owners, split reducer processor modules, and `grounding.oracle.DIMENSIONS`. Delete old aliases only when both semantic references and raw dynamic/string/monkeypatch census are empty.\n\n## Scope\n\n- CLI help aliases\n- code-review detector, graph/reducer, and grounding compatibility bindings\n- every source/test/patch/dynamic consumer\n\n## Testing\n\nRun targeted CLI/help, security-detector, graph/reducer, and grounding suites plus semantic and raw reference censuses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Each listed old private name is absent after all consumers migrate to its named canonical owner.\n- [x] Tests patch or import only canonical owners.\n- [x] Public CLI behavior, security detector results, graph reduction, reducer events, and grounding dimensions remain unchanged.\n- [x] Focused suites and complete semantic/raw reference scans pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788577225846332001,"uuid":"10964013-6957-41ae-85c3-535d7175a36b"}